  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1209 AM PM CST Sun Nov 8 2026 \n\nConditions ideal for radiational cooling are developing as\nexpected across the area tonight. Some sites are already below\nfreezing and those that aren't stand a very good chance of \nmaking it below by sunrise with a heavy killing frost. The \nfreeze warning will remain in place til the morning and this \nshould be the last one necessary for the year as the growing \nseason should be definitively over by the time this back to back\nheavy frost period ends. Ground fog is possible with soil \ntemperatures in the low 50s and residual warm water \ntemperatures.\n\nThe next item of interest presents on Wednesday. The guidance\nsuite is in considerably better agreement tonight on a fairly\nbroad upper trough digging in from the northwest and spinning up\na 1002-1004mb surface low that tracks across the northeastern\nquarter of the region as a strong cold front storms in behind.\nRainfall looks increasingly likely with amounts on deterministic\nand ensemble blends ranging from one-quarter to one-half inch.\nThe source airmass behind this front is in northern Canada where\nit is currently around -10F so this may be the first pseudo-\narctic airmass of the cool season and Thursday and Friday at\nleast look likely to be at least a little below seasonal norms.\nTo add to matters northwest winds 10-20 mph are shown by most\navailable guidance and make sense given the synoptic situation,\nso it will feel even colder.",
